<Base title="About" description="Backend developer in Ibadan, Nigeria. Computer Science student at Bowen University.">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p>
      I'm a backend developer in Ibadan, Nigeria, and a Computer Science student at Bowen University. I write Python
      services: APIs, retrieval pipelines for LLM apps, and the data layer underneath them.
    </p>

    <h2>What I've built</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Bowen AI.</strong> A study assistant for students. It answers from course documents and cites its
        sources. FastAPI, Qdrant, Gemini.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Amok AI.</strong> A multi-tenant AI platform: PostgreSQL schema design, tiered pricing logic, cost and
        margin modeling, and a RAG pipeline that keeps each tenant's data isolated.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Jarvis.</strong> The backend for an AI assistant: request routing, session logic, LLM integration and a
        RAG pipeline for document-grounded answers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vergold Technologies, April to August 2025.</strong> Software development intern. I helped build backend
        APIs with FastAPI and Flask, wrote internal tools and scripts in Python, and took part in code reviews.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What I work with</h2>
    <p>
      Python, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, SQLAlchemy, Qdrant, pgvector, JWT authentication, Docker, and the Groq,
      OpenAI and Hugging Face APIs.
    </p>

    <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
    <p>
      An internship or junior backend role on a team working with APIs, vector search or LLM infrastructure. I'm also
      open to freelance backend work.
    </p>

    <h2>Working with me</h2>
    <p>
      Email me at <a href="mailto:badmussamad13@gmail.com">badmussamad13@gmail.com</a> with what you need built or the
      role you're hiring for. My <a href="/resume.pdf">resume</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Samd43366">GitHub</a>
      are linked from every page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
